From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:18:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 107/109] net: mtk_eth_soc: optimize RX DMA header-only L1 cache prefetch (zero-stall QDMA IRQ)

Optimizes `mtk_poll_rx()` in `drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c` by
prefetching only the first 64-byte cacheline (`net_prefetch(pkt_data)`) during
RX DMA ring polling so the 32 KB MIPS 1004Kc L1 D-cache is never polluted with
payload bytes destined for PCIe Wi-Fi DMA, while keeping `MTK_QDMA_DELAY_INT = 0`
so single ARP, DHCP, and EAPOL handshake packets never wait in the QDMA ring.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -2012,6 +2012,7 @@ static int mtk_poll_rx(struct napi_struct *napi, int budget,
 		pkt_data = page_address(page) + trxd.rxd1;
 		dma_sync_single_for_cpu(eth->dma_dev, trxd.rxd1,
 					pkt_len, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
+		net_prefetch(pkt_data);
 
 		skb = build_skb(pkt_data, PAGE_SIZE);
